  "schematicNotes": [
    {
      "id": "n_cabinpower",
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 5910,
        "y": 0
      },
      "text": "CABIN POWER HARNESS - non-ECU: the two glove-box fuse + relay boxes of DECISIONS R75 (cad/fusebox rev 5, layout accepted by Dan 2026-10-14 (B6 = A); approval waits for every part to be a real buyable part (OPEN-ITEMS row 107); slot map in cad/fusebox/ST185-fusebox-summary.html): the POWER box (fb_power - copper bar fed 1/0 from the PDB bus, 7 AMI IN feeding the Mini ISO relays R1-R6, 7 AMI OUT, the ACPS mini fuse; outboard) and the LOGIC box (fb_logic - Bus 1 permanent from AMI OUT-1 BUS1 50A, Bus 2 switched from k_efi 87, mini fuses BUS1-n / BUS2-n, micro relays M11-M22; inboard). Both boxes live only in this file. Relays: k_htr R1, k_efi R2, k_str R3, k_fan R4, k_fan2 R5, k_pwr R6 (POWER); k_hl M11, k_hr M12, k_horn M13, k_etb M14, k_acc M15, k_eps_en M21, k_rev M22 (LOGIC); k_eps HCR150 beside the POWER box. The fuel pump relay k_fp is NOT here: it sits in the battery relay block in the trunk (ST185-HeavyDC); only its coil + (SW12) leaves this file, broken off (br_fp86). Each relay terminal is crimped and pushed into its printed cavity (no relay sockets); each relay feed is a cable from its AMI IN lug to terminal 30. The non-ECU relay coil circuits follow the EWD 1993 (k_hl / k_hr coil- to IE1-2 R-Y, p.116; k_horn coil- to IE1-19 G, p.185; k_htr coil from the old R/B4 R-L / L-W leads to the A/C amplifier HR, p.215; k_pwr coil+ key IG from the old R/B2 L-Y lead, p.137). The ECU coil (85) wires stay on ST185-A-cabin / ST185-B-cabin (their ECU pin sets the loom) and arrive broken off. Every feed between this file and another is drawn broken off in both with a note naming the other file. Gauges are this drawing's; the CAD summary's gauges are placeholders by fuse rating."
    },
    {
      "id": "n_cavity_notes",
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 5910,
        "y": 900
      },
      "text": "CAVITY NOTES - full text of the signals marked * on this drawing\nLOGIC EFI86 (BUS1-1): ATM-5 relay coil feed, PERMANENT (EFI main relay 86)\nLOGIC MRS IN / MRS (BUS2-12): ATM-7.5 MRS EPS pump logic enable, fed from k_eps_en 87 - this fuse position must NOT pick up the Bus 2 strip (OPEN-ITEMS, CAD detail work)\nLOGIC B30 IN / B30 (BUS2-13): ATM-2 start request, fed from the ignition switch ST1 tap - this fuse position must NOT pick up the Bus 2 strip (same)\nPOWER AMI OUT-6: AMI-60 EPS pump relay 30 (k_eps HCR150, beside the box), Bussmann AMI-60 (60 A, sized 2026-09-28 - sot/channels.csv k_eps c1)\nEFI Main Relay 85: ACTIVE-LOW Coil - -> Aux 6 / A28 - low-side (Aux 5-8 capable of either; low-side chosen for ECU Hold Power)\nEFI Main Relay 86: Coil + - PERMANENT battery via LOGIC EFI86 5A (must stay live after key-off for Hold Power)\nETB Power Relay 85: ACTIVE-LOW Coil - -> Aux 2 / A20 - LOW-SIDE ONLY (Aux 1-4)\nETB Power Relay 86: Coil + - ignition-switched 12V (EFI main relay 87)\nRadiator Fan Relay (on/off) 86: Coil + - ignition-switched 12V (EFI main relay 87)\nStart Relay 86: Coil + - ignition-switched 12V (EFI main relay 87)\nCondenser Fan Relay (on/off) 85: ACTIVE-LOW Coil - -> Ign 5 / B13 - low-side, no external flywheel diode or suppression (on/off relay; INFERENCE from the G4X help Auxiliary Output Wiring PWM-only diode advice, not a Link statement) - TE 1-1393304-0, plain relay, no diode\nCondenser Fan Relay (on/off) 86: Coil + - ignition-switched 12V (EFI main relay 87)\nMR-S EHPS pump relay k_eps 85: coil - <- MR-S pump B5 (br_w_eps_rly, bulkhead A c27); coil + on SW12 (R22)\nMR-S EHPS pump relay k_eps 30: POWER AMI OUT-6 - Bussmann AMI-60 (60 A, sized 2026-09-28 - sot/channels.csv k_eps c1)\nHeater relay k_htr 87: two wires in one 9.5 receptacle (8 AWG blower + 14 AWG ACPS feed) - receptacle TBD (OPEN-ITEMS)"
    }
  ],
